---
source: Hack the Box
title: Layover
difficulty: medium
tags: WiFi, Craft CMS, Decryption, CUPS
summary: The pentester is given initial credentials to perform a security test on HTB International. After gaining access to the machine, the attacker can sniff the wireless traffic and capture user credentials which allows them to gain access to the portal's admin panel. The site is using Craft CMS which is vulnerable to command injection. The attacker can abuse this to execute code on the webserver and gain access. Database credentials are found and the source code of the web app allows the attacker to construct the decryption logic and obtain another users credentials. After pivoting to the new user, a vulnerable CUPS service can be exploited to gain root access and fully compromise the machine.
---

> As is common in real life pentests, you will start the Layover box with credentials for the following account contractor / Contractor2026!

## [01] Port Scan and Service Discovery
```term
$ sudo nmap -p- -sC -sV -oN scans/nmap_all_tcp.txt 10.129.94.240

PORT     STATE SERVICE       REASON         VERSION
