With our given credentials, we can attempt to RDP into the machine.

## [02] Finding Credentials, Compromising the Portal Web Server

The credentials allow us to access the machine. Opening a terminal and checking for user privileges shows the following:
```term
$ contractor@airside-ws01:~$ sudo -l
[sudo] password for contractor: 
Matching Defaults entries for contractor on airside-ws01:
    env_reset, mail_badpass,
    secure_path=/usr/local/sbin\:/usr/local/bin\:/usr/sbin\:/usr/bin\:/sbin\:/bin\:/snap/bin,
    use_pty

User contractor may run the following commands on airside-ws01:
!!    (ALL : ALL) ALL
```

We have root access to this machine. Opening the web browser shows a landing page with `wifi.international.htb`. We can also see on the Desktop interface that we currently do not have an active wifi connection.
We can verify by checking our interface configuration.
```term
$ root@airside-ws01:~# ifconfig
